WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.620
How big a role will the Wild Hunt play in&nbsp;
the third season of "The Witcher"? Why is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.940
Yen wearing that familiar mask? And&nbsp;
is that Nibbles? Here are the small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.000
details you missed in the teaser&nbsp;
for season three of "The Witcher."

00:00:12.805 --> 00:00:15.865
The Season 3 teaser for "The&nbsp;
Wicher" begins with an ominous line:

00:00:15.865 --> 00:00:24.000
"Now, for the first time, I understand real fear."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.180
It's a heavy statement coming from a Witcher, and&nbsp;
especially the eternally stoic Geralt of Rivia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.920
Though he's a magically-enhanced, superpowered&nbsp;
monster hunter who's lost at least some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.500
his humanity, Geralt is obviously not entirely&nbsp;
emotionless. It's just that as a general rule,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.940
he likes to play his cards close to his&nbsp;
chest. Even so, fear hasn't ever really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.920
been part of the package. After all, scared&nbsp;
Witchers tend to be dead Witchers. So, what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.300
is the thing that could frighten a guy who fights&nbsp;
gigantic, overpowered abominations for a living?

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.500
Though the trailer frames Geralt's fear as&nbsp;
something that's related to a particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.300
mighty opponent, it also makes clear that&nbsp;
Ciri and possibly Yennefer are in danger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.940
as well. He might have his&nbsp;
issues with his former lover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.260
but Geralt has a close connection to both&nbsp;
women. The fear he admits to may very well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.640
be for their well-being instead of his own.&nbsp;
Here's hoping it turns out to be unfounded.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.280
Apocalypses are often heralded by foreboding&nbsp;
figures. In the world of "The Witcher," the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.960
supposed harbingers of calamity take the&nbsp;
form of mysterious riders from an alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.280
dimension. These riders are known as the&nbsp;
"Wild Hunt," and audiences were treated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.180
to a glimpse of them at the end of Season&nbsp;
2. In the final episode, Geralt, Yennefer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.040
and Ciri come face to face with the leader&nbsp;
of the Wild Hunt in their nightmarish realm.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:46.440
"Child of the Elder Blood, starry eyed&nbsp;
daughter of chaos. Join the Hunt."

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.340
Although the trio of heroes manages to&nbsp;
escape from this plane of existence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.260
the Wild Hunt craves the blood of Ciri. It's why&nbsp;
they chase after her in the trailer for Season 3.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.220
Their hunt for her is because Ciri has&nbsp;
access to ancient and long-forgotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.220
magic. The riders of the Wild&nbsp;
Hunt believe her abilities will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.120
save their accursed dimension from&nbsp;
obliteration. Powerful and deadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.920
the Wild Hunt will probably be a major focus for&nbsp;
Season 3 of "The Witcher," especially considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.180
that some of their history was expounded on in&nbsp;
the prequel series "The Witcher: Blood Origin."

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:20.820
Also known as the Wraiths of Morhogg, the Wild&nbsp;
Hunt is led by the elf Eredin. All of the Wild&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:26.160
Hunt members are elves, and they were created as&nbsp;
a means to procure slave labor from other planes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.380
of existence. Their purpose gave rise to their&nbsp;
status as heartless reavers. Hopefully, Geralt is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:36.854
up to the task when it comes to defending Ciri and&nbsp;
defeating these long-lived extra-planar raiders.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.380
It looks like Geralt is out for&nbsp;
blood in "The Witcher" Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.460
but at least he's taken the time to prepare his&nbsp;
gear for the adventure. Early in the trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:49.620
we get a nice action shot of the Witcher pulling&nbsp;
out his steel sword. Eagle-eyed fans may notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.900
it now features a line of runes running down the&nbsp;
middle and a beautiful green-glowing stone fixed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.680
to the guard. While these weapon enhancements&nbsp;
don't feature in "The Witcher" book series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.580
avid fans of the video games will&nbsp;
quickly recognize the upgrade system.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.200
Since the first release, runestones have been&nbsp;
fixtures of "The Witcher" video games. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.640
In "The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt," developers&nbsp;
CD Projekt Red took it to the next level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.920
introducing Lesser Runes, Runes, and Greater&nbsp;
Runes. When equipped, runestones offer different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.780
boosts to Geralt's attacks, like a chance to&nbsp;
burn or cause bleeding. They also change the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.160
appearance of the weapons, with colored runes&nbsp;
running down the length of the blades. It looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.831
like "The Witcher" Season 3 will introduce that&nbsp;
upgrade system in some form to Geralt's weapons.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:35.700
As Geralt prepares for battle against a shadowy&nbsp;
figure that stands in the hall in front of him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.480
he drinks one of his many potions to&nbsp;
power up. The Witcher only imbibes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.960
these deadly concoctions when he&nbsp;
absolutely needs to, it's clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.640
that he's facing a truly dangerous enemy.&nbsp;
But who or what is he actually up against?

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.600
The figure is blurry enough to keep&nbsp;
things delightfully mysterious. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.940
since they wear dark clothes, it's easy to assume&nbsp;
that they're either a member of the Wild Hunt or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:02.400
perhaps a Nilfgaardian soldier. However, there's&nbsp;
another powerful force that favors black armor and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:08.160
is at odds with Geralt: his fellow Witchers. After&nbsp;
Vesemir discovers that Geralt's ward Ciri could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.780
the key to restoring Witchers to their former&nbsp;
glory, he may want to claim Ciri for himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:18.660
If so, Geralt drawing his sword is a pretty clear&nbsp;
hint that the negotiations aren't going very well.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.940
Another possible identity for the shadowy&nbsp;
figure is none other than the mage Vilgefortz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.581
who has gained more power within the brotherhood&nbsp;
and may also be setting his sights on Ciri.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:33.060
Rience returns in Season 3 with a&nbsp;
vengeance. At the end of Season 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.060
the assassin is on the verge of&nbsp;
discovering who actually hired him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:40.260
to pursue Ciri. He returns in the&nbsp;
teaser in a familiar halo of fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:44.760
but that doesn't mean his appearance is more of&nbsp;
the same. The new season could bring clarity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.380
some of his biggest unanswered questions,&nbsp;
particularly the mystery of who hired him.

00:04:49.511 --> 00:04:51.977
"What do you want?" "To meet your employer."

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:58.620
The obvious identity of Rience's employer may be&nbsp;
Emhyr or even Stregobor, but the books reveal him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:03.360
to be someone else entirely. Though currently an&nbsp;
ally in the show, Rience's master in the novels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.340
is none other than Vilgefortz. The mage who&nbsp;
helped defend Sodden Hill against Nilfgaard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:13.094
Vilgefortz has ulterior motives that are&nbsp;
only now starting to come to the surface.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.820
In one of the trailer's blink-or-you'll-miss-it&nbsp;
moments, Yennefer can be seen looking for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.540
Geralt in a dark, torch-lit room. When&nbsp;
she turns around, it's revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:25.740
she's wearing a mask. Eagle-eyed fans will&nbsp;
remember the mask from a previous episode.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.840
The Season 1 episode "Bottled Appetites" sees&nbsp;
Yennefer set out to restore her fertility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:36.180
but the most memorable scene involves her using&nbsp;
magic to conjure up a risqué party in a mansion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.680
When Geralt and Jaskier find her later on,&nbsp;
she's sitting amid a sea of naked bodies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.520
watching the erotic events from&nbsp;
behind a lace mask. The mask in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.880
the Season 3 trailer appears to be the&nbsp;
very same one she wore in that episode.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:52.380
It's unknown at this time as to why Yennefer&nbsp;
puts on a mask and goes running around dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:57.120
rooms in Season 3. But the mask is synonymous&nbsp;
with one of Season 1's most memorable episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.168
and it teases another night of&nbsp;
unpredictability next season.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:07.680
"The Witcher 3: The Wild Hunt" can be described&nbsp;
in one word: massive. The open-world game boasts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.360
close to 200 hours of gameplay. In it you play&nbsp;
as Geralt, trying to find a way to save his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:17.220
surrogate daughter from the titular Wild Hunt.&nbsp;
With such an expansive landscape, there are many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:21.660
characters in play. So it's no surprise that&nbsp;
Netflix's "The Witcher" has only scratched the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:26.160
surface of the franchise's iconic characters.&nbsp;
The new teaser is a window to one character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.320
only briefly featured in the series so far,&nbsp;
Philippa Eilhart. A contemporary of Yennefer's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:37.020
Philippa appears in Season 2, mostly to assist&nbsp;
spymaster Dijkstra. But if the source material&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:41.700
is any indication, there's much more in store for&nbsp;
the next appearance of this powerful sorceress.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:46.140
In the teaser, Jaskier appears on the wrong&nbsp;
end of a sharp-looking ring that resembles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:51.000
a talon. Philippa's affinity for transforming&nbsp;
into an owl makes her the likely perpetrator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.020
indicating she will be a player in&nbsp;
Season 3. Like most sorceresses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:59.400
she is not all that she appears to be.&nbsp;
Though sometimes affiliated with Dijkstra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:04.140
she always has an agenda and uses her powers&nbsp;
as a political tool to achieve her goals.

00:07:04.345 --> 00:07:08.545
"Bring me the bard. It's about&nbsp;
time he paid back his benefactor."

00:07:08.545 --> 00:07:12.000
Jaskier has a close connection&nbsp;
to Ciri, meaning he may be an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.284
obstacle for vicious Philippa to get&nbsp;
her hands on the young powerhouse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.284 --> 00:07:19.784
The mage's lust for power is only one&nbsp;
of her dastardly personality traits.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:24.360
"The Witcher" Season 2 saw Ciri&nbsp;
live and train in Kaer Morhen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.900
where she learned how to become a noble&nbsp;
warrior like the witchers of the School&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.620
of the Wolf. However, that's nothing&nbsp;
compared to being at the center of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:35.040
Continent-wide hunt that brings out the&nbsp;
most formidable killers in the world.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.540
The upcoming season of "The Witcher" is going&nbsp;
to be eventful for Ciri, and that's putting it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:44.220
mildly. Every mage, monarch, and monster&nbsp;
of the Continent is out to capture her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.600
and she'll only be able to hide for so long&nbsp;
before she has to face these demons. One of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.560
the storylines will see her become separated&nbsp;
from her guardians, which is evident in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.760
latest trailer. The Continent is a nasty&nbsp;
world at the best of times, let alone when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:00.840
the Wild Hunt returns. Chances are good that&nbsp;
she'll encounter trouble at every corner.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:05.340
Toward the end of the trailer, we see Yennefer,&nbsp;
Geralt, and Ciri wandering around in the dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:09.900
completely separated from each other. The&nbsp;
threat of danger looms large and it's clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:14.040
that something is about to go down. Ciri being&nbsp;
on her own indicates that she's going to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.180
to put her training to good use sooner&nbsp;
rather than later. Geralt and Yennefer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:22.997
will undoubtedly lend a hand, but Ciri will need&nbsp;
to come into her own if she's going to survive.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:27.840
In the video game "The Witcher 3: Wild&nbsp;
Hunt," players meet an unusual cat who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.460
sits on a table cleaning itself, stopping&nbsp;
occasionally to stare at Geralt. Cats are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:36.360
unique in the universe of "The Witcher." They&nbsp;
can soak up magic in a way no one else can,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:41.460
except maybe a Witcher. Cats hate Witchers,&nbsp;
which is what makes this cat such an anomaly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:45.660
Nicknamed Nibbles, his appearance in the&nbsp;
Season 3 trailer comes as a welcome surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:51.660
given his origin. CD Projekt Red cinematic&nbsp;
artist Kajetan Kapuściński told Kotaku,

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:56.400
"The truth is Nibbles was born as a filmmaking&nbsp;
trick due to a technical necessity that came up."

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.660
During a crucial meeting in the video game, the&nbsp;
game designers decided they wanted something to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:05.640
distract gamers for a short time. The decision to&nbsp;
add a cat was a practical and strategic decision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.240
but theories started on the internet&nbsp;
that claimed the cat was a shapeshifter.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:14.880
Alas, Nibbles is just a cat, but he's continued to&nbsp;
show up in random game scenes. Kapuściński said,

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.360
"We never expected the few appearances&nbsp;
it makes in 'Wild Hunt' to be noticed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:21.240
We've put that cat through a lot&nbsp;
of life-threatening situations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:25.500
and it's been there as a brave observer of&nbsp;
Geralt's story unfolding before players."

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.260
Now that he's officially part of&nbsp;
the Netflix "The Witcher" series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:31.983
we hope he becomes just as endearing&nbsp;
as his video game counterpart.

